And v5.0 should have this invariant:

> A new machine can identify itself, resolve its profile, converge to desired configuration, verify the result, detect drift, and safely repeat the entire operation without producing unintended state changes.



That's the point where this stops being merely a sophisticated dotfiles repository and becomes a small, reusable configuration-management platform—which is much more aligned with the agentic/reusable-workflow directions you're pursuing I'm in.
